{"id":"NCT07285018","title":"A Chronic Pain Master Protocol (CPMP): A Study of LY4065967 in Participants With Diabetic Peripheral Neuropathic Pain","official":"Randomized, Placebo-Controlled, Phase 2 Clinical Trial to Evaluate LY4065967 for the Treatment of Diabetic Peripheral Neuropathic Pain","summary":"The purpose of this study is to test the safety and efficacy of study drug LY4065967 for the treatment of diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain (DPNP). This trial is part of the chronic pain master protocol H0P-MC-CPMP (NCT05986292) which is a protocol to accelerate the development of new treatments for chronic pain.","conditions":["Diabetic Peripheral Neuropathic Pain"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"LY4065967"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have presence of diabetic peripheral neuropathy, of symmetrical nature and in lower extremities for ≥6 months and diagnosed by a score of Part B ≥3 on Michigan Neuropathy Screening Instrument (©University of Michigan)\n* Have a history and current diagnosis of type 1 or type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n* Have an HbA1c \\<11% and on a stable regimen for treatment of diabetes at least 90 days prior to screening\n* Have a body mass index at screening of ≤40 kilogram per meter squared (kg/m2)\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Are pregnant or breastfeeding\n* Have a history of other potentially causative and/or confounding sources of pain that may impair self-assessment of pain due to diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain (DPNP)\n* Have lower limb amputation due to diabetes inclusive of great toe (metatarsal bone)\n* Have serum vitamin B12 ≤200 picogram per milliliter (pg/mL)\n* Have an abnormal BP (systolic BP \\>140 mm Hg and diastolic BP\\>90 mm Hg) at screening\n* Have history or current clinically significant cardiac disease, including arrhythmia, aortic aneurysm, heart failure, current electrolyte abnormalities, or any other conditions that could predispose to arrhythmia in the judgement of the investigator","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":150,"start":"2026-02-16","pcd":"2027-07","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","areas":["neurology"],"central":["Trial questions or participation questions: 1-877-CTLILLY (1-877-285-4559) or · 1-317-615-4559 · LillyTrials@Lilly.com","Physicians interested in becoming principal investigators please contact · clinical_inquiry_hub@lilly.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Central Research Associates","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35205","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":""},{"f":"Synexus Clinical Research US, Inc.","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85020","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"Arizona Research Center","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85053","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"Desert Oasis Healthcare Medical Group","city":"Palm Springs","pr":"California","zip":"92262","s":"R","lat":33.8303,"lon":-116.5453,"c":""},{"f":"Artemis Institute for Clinical Research","city":"Riverside","pr":"California","zip":"92503","s":"R","lat":33.9534,"lon":-117.3962,"c":""},{"f":"Artemis Institute for Clinical Research","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":""},{"f":"CMR of Greater New Haven","city":"Hamden","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06517","s":"R","lat":41.3959,"lon":-72.8968,"c":""},{"f":"Bradenton Research Center, Inc.","city":"Bradenton","pr":"Florida","zip":"34205","s":"R","lat":27.4989,"lon":-82.5748,"c":""},{"f":"Accel Research Sites - DeLand Clinical Research Unit","city":"DeLand","pr":"Florida","zip":"32720","s":"R","lat":29.0283,"lon":-81.3031,"c":""},{"f":"K2 MEDICAL Research THE VILLAGES","city":"Lady Lake","pr":"Florida","zip":"32159","s":"R","lat":28.9175,"lon":-81.9229,"c":""},{"f":"K2 Medical Research ORLANDO","city":"Maitland","pr":"Florida","zip":"32751","s":"R","lat":28.6278,"lon":-81.3631,"c":""},{"f":"